; PolyField Track — Start List BACKUP LSS
; Redundant start-list output. FinishLynx sends the start list only once (on event
; load / gun) with no refresh, so a single dropped datagram leaves it blank until a
; manual re-send. Configure this script as a SECOND Network (UDP) scoreboard output,
; also targeting the PolyField machine on port 5001, so the start list is transmitted
; TWICE as two independent datagrams. If one is lost to packet loss, the other still
; delivers it.
;
; PolyField treats every startlist-event| header as a fresh full broadcast and
; de-duplicates athletes by lane, so the second (duplicate) copy is harmless — it
; simply rebuilds the same list, or fills it in if the first copy was lost.
;
; Use ALONGSIDE polyfield.lss (the primary all-in-one output). This script sends
; ONLY the start list — no clock, wind, or results — to keep the extra traffic minimal.
;
; FinishLynx Scoreboard Configuration (second output):
;   Script:      polyfield-backup.lss
;   Port:        Network (UDP)
;   IP Address:  <PolyField machine IP>   (same as the primary output)
;   Port Number: 5001

;;StartListHeader
\13\00startlist-event|
\13\02%s
\13\00|round=
\13\05%s
\13\00|heat=
\13\06%s
\13\00|eventno=
\13\04%s\r\n

;;StartList
\14\00startlist|lane=
\14\02%s
\14\00|bib=
\14\03%s
\14\00|first=
\14\17%s
\14\00|last=
\14\18%s
\14\00|club=
\14\05%s\r\n

;;StartedHeader
\13\00startlist-event|
\13\02%s
\13\00|round=
\13\05%s
\13\00|heat=
\13\06%s
\13\00|eventno=
\13\04%s\r\n

;;Started
\14\00startlist|lane=
\14\02%s
\14\00|bib=
\14\03%s
\14\00|first=
\14\17%s
\14\00|last=
\14\18%s
\14\00|club=
\14\05%s\r\n

;;ResultsTrailer
\13\00results-end\r\n
